<library>
<description>Senba BS612 digital pyroelectric infrared (PIR) sensor, LCSC C389589.

Land pattern and pin numbering transcribed from the EasyEDA library for C389589 --
the pattern JLCPCB assemble against. Pin names confirmed against the datasheet,
[`../../datasheets/pir-BS612.pdf`](../../datasheets/pir-BS612.pdf) p.8:
  1 SENS   2 OEN   3 VSS   4 VDD   5 REL   6 ONTIME

Six 0.914 mm holes on a TO-5 pin circle, dia 9.2 mm can. Supply 2.2-3.7 V
(typ 3.0), 9.5 uA. REL drives +/-10 mA, so it goes straight to a GPIO.

THIS SENSOR HAS NO OPTICS. Bare it reaches about a metre; the range and the
coverage pattern come entirely from the Fresnel lens (SB-F-02, LCSC C89924,
focal length 11.5 mm, 120 deg, 10 m). The lens is also the window - HDPE passes
8-14 um, ordinary plastic and acrylic do not. JLCPCB stock the lens but cannot
fit it: no footprint, so no CPL entry. It is an enclosure part.

Datasheet rules that bear on layout, and that conflict with this board:
  - keep its connections short, and route NOTHING underneath them, high-current
    traces least of all. The NeoPixel ring and both digit chains are exactly that.
  - give it its own ground island, tied to the board by only +, - and output.
  - 100 nF from VDD to GND as close to pin 4 as it will go. Not optional.
  - keep it away from U2: the MiCS heater is 76 mW and pyroelectric sensors
    respond to thermal drift.
  - do not wash the assembled board; cleaning fluid wicking into the lens
    degrades it permanently.
  - hand-solder at &lt;=350 C for &lt;=3 s; wave soldering may degrade it.</description>
<packages>
<package name="SENSORM-TH_BS612">
<description>BS612 PIR, TO-5 6-pin, dia 9.2 mm can, 0.914 mm drills</description>
<pad name="1" x="2.7" y="1.1151" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<pad name="2" x="2.7" y="-1.1151" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<pad name="3" x="1.08" y="-2.7" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<pad name="4" x="-2.7" y="-1.1151" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<pad name="5" x="-2.7" y="1.1151" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<pad name="6" x="-1.0399" y="2.7201" drill="0.914" diameter="1.524" shape="round"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="4.6" width="0.2" layer="21"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="4.6" width="0.127" layer="51"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="4.85" width="0.05" layer="39"/>
<text x="-4.6" y="5.3" size="1.27" layer="25">&gt;NAME</text>
<text x="-4.6" y="-6.6" size="1.27" layer="27">&gt;VALUE</text>
<wire x1="4.9" y1="1.1151" x2="6.1" y2="1.1151" width="0.2" layer="21"/>
</package>
</packages>
